💥 What is AWS Load Balancer?
A Load Balancer is like a traffic controller for your servers. It helps divide incoming traffic across multiple servers so that no single server gets overloaded.

Why Use a Load Balancer🤔 :
🔹 Distributes incoming traffic across multiple servers
🔹 Prevents any single server from getting overloaded
🔹 Keeps applications fast and responsive under heavy load
🔹 Provides high availability by routing traffic only to healthy servers
🔹 Automatically detects and avoids failed servers

➤ Types of AWS Load Balancers :

1. Application Load Balancer (ALB) :
 → Best for web applications and micro-services(works with HTTP/HTTPS)
 → Routes traffic based on URL, headers, etc.

2. Network Load Balancer (NLB) :
 → For high-performance, low-latency traffic
 → Works at the network level (TCP/UDP)

3. Gateway Load Balancer (GLB): 
 → Sends traffic through third-party tools like firewalls
 → Good for adding security appliances

💥 Real-time scenario for an E-commerce🛍️ site using AWS Load Balancer:

🛒 An E-commerce website hosted on AWS uses an Application Load Balancer (ALB) to manage high traffic during sales. It distributes user requests across multiple servers, ensuring fast loading and no downtime.

⚙️ How the Load Balancer Works:

 → User sends a request to the Load Balancer 🎯
 → Load Balancer acts as a traffic controller.
 → It checks the health of all app servers 🖥️
 → Routes traffic only to healthy & available servers.
 → Ignores unhealthy or overloaded servers ❌
